WEBVTT

00:20.960 --> 00:22.920
I don't see anything here.

00:22.920 --> 00:23.820
Yeah.

00:29.710 --> 00:31.330
Itchy, itchy, itchy!

00:31.330 --> 00:32.380
Itchy!

00:32.380 --> 00:34.310
Itchy, itchy, itchy!

00:34.310 --> 00:35.130
What's going on?!

00:35.130 --> 00:36.130
7G!

00:36.130 --> 00:36.960
Is making us itchy?!

00:36.960 --> 00:38.370
Damn you, Higashi-Kurume!

00:38.370 --> 00:39.630
This is the worst one yet!

00:39.630 --> 00:41.350
Nadeko-chan, up the speed!

00:41.350 --> 00:42.250
I'm so itchy, I can't!

00:42.250 --> 00:44.170
Dying! Dying!

01:09.810 --> 01:12.330
Are we okay this time?

01:15.140 --> 01:16.950
Looks like it.

01:21.750 --> 01:23.740
No! That was beyond my control!

01:23.740 --> 01:24.430
I'm sorry!

01:24.430 --> 01:26.100
Sorry for turning a blind eye!

01:26.100 --> 01:26.720
I really am!

01:26.720 --> 01:27.960
Mr. Badger! Mr. Badger!

01:27.960 --> 01:30.110
Please rest in peace, Mr. Badger!

01:31.280 --> 01:33.740
Dad! Come back, Dad!

01:33.740 --> 01:36.120
I should have stopped you two 
from arguing back then!

01:59.260 --> 02:03.060
<b>Train to the End of the World</b>

03:17.380 --> 03:18.750
Onward, Apogee!

03:18.750 --> 03:20.310
Go east!

03:20.310 --> 03:21.500
You sure are excited.

03:20.880 --> 03:26.390
Episode 8       Isn't That Bad Karma?

03:21.500 --> 03:22.610
Well, duh.

03:22.610 --> 03:24.890
Remember what that weird 
old guy in Hoya said?

03:24.890 --> 03:26.450
<i>NeriAli</i>'s up ahead!

03:26.450 --> 03:27.690
Was he telling the truth?

03:27.690 --> 03:30.370
Did Oizumi-gakuen really 
turn into <i>NeriAli</i> Land?

03:30.370 --> 03:32.080
It's the 7G incident.

03:32.080 --> 03:33.270
Anything goes.

03:33.270 --> 03:36.220
I guess we have run into a lot 
of far-fetched things so far.

03:36.220 --> 03:37.020
Right, right?

03:37.020 --> 03:41.030
<b>Darkizumites
Denizens of Dark Nerima. Kindhearted, gentle, and hate conflict. As a result, they end up
oppressed by Chaos and his men. Used to be normal humans, but their extreme dependency
has slowly turned them pig-like. It's said that too much dependency can turn them
into full-blown pigs, but none of them seem to care. They're really fine with that?
A great number of them love beef.</b>

03:37.020 --> 03:41.030
Everyone in Oizumi-gakuen turned 
into the Darkizumites from <i>NeriAli</i>.

03:41.030 --> 03:41.860
<b>Alice
Mischievous third-year in high school who went through the
roller coaster that is: No. 2 in the school hierarchy -> Complete recluse ->
Young leader of Dark Nerima. Searching online for the incident that
turned her into a recluse still turns up hits, so don't look it up.
So what if she wet herself once? I'd even say a screw-up like that
is a must for a character brimming with charisma like Alice!
What do you think?</b>

03:41.030 --> 03:44.470
There's also people who became 
Alice, Iron Monty, Su-chan,

03:41.860 --> 03:42.950
<b>Iron Monty
\h
A professional torturer who keeps torture devices from all over the world
on hand. Has a great deal of pride. Hails from a long line of torturers.
Takes his work seriously, but sometimes loses himself to torturer's high
(ecstasy felt by torturers). Goes on about how at the heart of torture is a
relationship of trust between torturer and torturee. Whatever that means.</b>

03:42.950 --> 03:44.570
<b>Su-chan
Highly suicidal girl. Keeps a noose around her neck to die at any time
as part of her personal identity. Goes into a panic and faints when the
noose is taken off. She says it feels like walking in public naked.
Averse to hardship and adversity, she always complains with
"Dying, dying!" When something happens to her, gets angry with
"Are you trying to kill me?" Sings a weird song when she feels happy.
Wants to visit Sugamo Prison someday. It's gone, girl.</b>

03:44.470 --> 03:46.640
and even Opie, the opium poppy.

03:44.570 --> 03:46.240
<b>Opie
\h
An opium poppy come to life. Releases a white fluid when
under stress or beat to a pulp. This white fluid makes you
feel really, really good. All your worries melt away
and it feelsh like nuthin' mattersh. But no need fer worry.
The magic of genetic engineerin' meansh ya won't get
addicted. Heheh. Heheheheheh. Whew, feelsh like heaven. Urp.</b>

03:46.240 --> 03:52.460
<b>Alice in Nerima Land
Official Fanbook</b>

03:46.640 --> 03:49.020
I'm <i>so</i> jealous of whoever got to be Alice!

03:49.020 --> 03:52.950
Wait, that means we'll also run 
into Alice's nemesis, Chaos.

03:52.460 --> 03:53.460
<b>Chaos
Norfolk terrier. Boss of Dark Nerima, as you all know.
Bad to the bone. Loves decay and chaos above all.
Claims that Japanese wolves went extinct because he
devoured them all. Opposed to using violence to rule,
he's better at exploiting weaknesses and picking away
at them. Good at uncovering trauma and feels extreme
joy when degrading and humiliating others.
In short, this puppy's one big troublemaker.</b>

03:52.950 --> 03:55.390
Not only Chaos, but his 
minions Man-Cow, Rugger Man,

03:53.460 --> 03:54.710
<b>Man-Cow
An abomination that's part cow, part human.
Fires breast milk in all directions
and can't stop itself when it gets started.
Its breast milk is acidic and making contact
results in a furious itch, as well as mysterious
rashes. Has four all-season tires in place of legs
and can traverse any terrain. Fueled by breast milk,
of course. Extremely scared of weaning.</b>

03:54.710 --> 03:55.210
<b>Rugger Man
\h
A rugby player who wanted to be a baseball player, which
is why he uses baseball phrases like "Hey, batter batter"
or "nice swing". Has no love of rugby and doesn't care
if you mix it up with gridiron football. The canoe he rides
runs on hydropower. Slapping it makes it go faster, but if
it gets in a bad mood, sometimes it ignores Rugger Man
and speeds off wherever it likes (mainly down
Senkawa-dori and Kyuwaseda-dori).</b>

03:55.210 --> 03:55.960
<b>Calico Cat
A rare male calico. The one who brought Alice to Dark Nerima.
Calls himself a video game enthusiast. Never skips his workouts,
but aren't those muscles more of a turn-off? As for why he works out,
bluntly put, "So I can snatch new consoles and games and make a run
for it." Hates shooters, action games, RPGs, and simulation games.</b>

03:55.390 --> 03:57.840
Calico Cat, Jonidan, Guilt Incarnate,

03:55.960 --> 03:56.460
<b>Jonidan
The reincarnation of a jonidan sumo wrestler sacrificed to the gods.
The patterns on his body are said to be a vestige, but there are rumors
he drew them on himself. Look up "wicker man" for more details.
Regrets only making it to the jonidan division in sumo wrestling,
but there are no records to be found of him at all, so some think
he's just a chubby guy telling porkies.</b>

03:56.460 --> 03:57.840
<b>Guilt Incarnate
Just like his name says, the personification of all the guilt
in the world. From that, you'd think he'd be clingy, but he's
actually very easygoing. Obviously thinks saying sorry will
fix everything, which can get on your nerves. Sometimes
attacks by firing a guilt beam from his head. His guilt beam
is extremely sour. It's said to taste like black vinegar.</b>

03:57.840 --> 04:00.380
<b>Quarter Evening Cicada,
Quarter Brown Cicada, Et Cetera
Claims to be an elite specimen with all the best traits of cicadas,
but he's really just a mixed breed. Rare example of a cicada bad
at playing dead who gets found out instantly. Constantly receives
stern warnings from the All-Japan Association of Cicadas Playing
Dead. Despite this, he's always caught off guard and is easily
tricked by other cicadas playing dead. His hilarious reactions
are a big hit with the crowd.</b>

03:57.840 --> 04:00.630
Quarter Evening Cicada, 
Quarter Brown Cicada, Et Cetera,

04:00.380 --> 04:02.170
<b>Walkers
Shogi pawns. They talk with thick accents that have no rhyme
or reason to them. Very arrogant despite being weak.
They side with those stronger than them and lead carefree lives.</b>

04:00.630 --> 04:03.280
and the enemy grunts, the Walkers.

04:03.280 --> 04:04.930
I can't help but be scared.

04:04.930 --> 04:06.380
It's okay, Nadeko-chan.

04:06.380 --> 04:10.720
He said <i>NeriAli</i> World is set after 
the end of the series finale.

04:10.270 --> 04:14.520
<b>Episode 25

A Doggone Loser Yowls!
But Only the Norfolk Terrier</b>

04:10.270 --> 04:14.520
<b>Episode 25

A Doggone Loser Yowls!
But Only the Norfolk Terrier</b>

04:10.270 --> 04:14.520
<b>Top 3 Important Items in NeriAli</b>

04:10.270 --> 04:14.520
<b>Top 3 Important Items in NeriAli</b>

04:10.270 --> 04:14.520
<b>1. Fountain of Captured Pieces</b>

04:10.270 --> 04:14.520
<b>2. Russian Washlet</b>

04:10.270 --> 04:14.520
<b>3. Scythe</b>

04:10.720 --> 04:11.680
Oh, yeah.

04:11.680 --> 04:16.360
They defeat Chaos and the other bad guys 
and put them inside a shogi bag.

04:16.360 --> 04:17.270
Exactly.

04:17.270 --> 04:20.160
I feel sorry for the people 
who became Walkers.

04:20.160 --> 04:21.550
<i>Su-chan, you're too slow!</i>

04:21.550 --> 04:23.320
<i>Take that noose off already!</i>

04:23.320 --> 04:24.030
<i>Nuh-uh!</i>

04:24.030 --> 04:25.950
<i>I'll die if I take this off!</i>

04:25.950 --> 04:27.580
<i>It's my identity!</i>

04:26.450 --> 04:29.410
<i>If Man-Cow and the others catch us, 
we'll be put to death!</i>

04:29.410 --> 04:31.000
<i>We're dead either way!</i>

04:32.150 --> 04:33.120
<i>Iron Monty!</i>

04:33.120 --> 04:34.520
<i>You got it!</i>

04:36.720 --> 04:37.730
<i>Mon!</i>

04:38.160 --> 04:40.670
<i>Dying, dying, dying!</i>

04:40.670 --> 04:42.380
Does Iron Monty get off on hurting people?

04:42.380 --> 04:44.590
He used to be a pro torturer.

04:44.590 --> 04:46.940
He takes pride in his torture,

04:46.940 --> 04:50.180
but he hates being in pain himself.

04:50.180 --> 04:53.240
And Su-chan's the one who 
always attempts suicide?

04:53.240 --> 04:53.910
Yep.

04:53.910 --> 04:57.040
Opie's the one who spews 
freaky juice when hurt,

04:57.040 --> 04:59.580
which makes everyone feel good?

04:59.580 --> 05:03.590
Yeah, but it's been genetically 
altered to be harmless to humans.

05:03.590 --> 05:04.780
Oh, who's this guy?

05:04.780 --> 05:05.590
The boss?

05:05.590 --> 05:06.580
He's called Chaos.

05:06.580 --> 05:08.540
Because he KOs people with his stomping?

05:08.540 --> 05:11.860
I think that's a part of it, 
but it's written differently.

05:11.860 --> 05:13.740
The spelling is a little more difficult.

05:13.740 --> 05:14.720
<i>Look here.</i>

05:15.550 --> 05:19.120
<i>I came up with a </i>real<i> good idea last night.</i>

05:19.120 --> 05:22.210
It looks like Alice doesn't 
have any chance of winning.

05:22.210 --> 05:23.370
Don't worry.

05:23.370 --> 05:26.270
The world of Dark Oizumi 
may seem topsy-turvy,

05:26.270 --> 05:28.280
but it's all actually a shogi board.

05:28.280 --> 05:31.430
When all's said and done, they all 
have to obey the rules of shogi.

05:31.750 --> 05:34.360
And so, once Alice figures that out,

05:34.360 --> 05:37.240
she uses hasami shogi to 
take down Chaos and his men,

05:37.240 --> 05:39.160
leaving her free to return to Nerima.

05:39.160 --> 05:42.300
But then, you won't believe 
what happens next!

05:42.300 --> 05:43.130
Oh, no!

05:43.130 --> 05:45.330
I got carried away and started spoiling it!

05:45.330 --> 05:46.870
I'm so sorry!

05:46.870 --> 05:47.840
It's fine, really.

05:47.840 --> 05:48.780
I don't mind.

05:54.860 --> 05:57.530
Sounds like they're partying!

06:07.140 --> 06:08.150
Welcome, welcome!

06:08.150 --> 06:09.050
A crappy welcome to you!

06:09.050 --> 06:10.280
Everything's cheap, cheap!

06:10.280 --> 06:11.230
Cheap and shoddy!

06:11.220 --> 06:13.220
<b>Signature Gutton Candy</b>

06:11.220 --> 06:13.220
<b>Signature Gutton Candy</b>

06:11.230 --> 06:13.230
Die right up and have a look!

06:13.230 --> 06:15.310
Only 300 yen apiece!

06:15.310 --> 06:17.850
Ugh, why's this place full of Walkers?

06:17.850 --> 06:20.010
I don't see any Darkizumites.

06:20.010 --> 06:21.510
You're right. But why?

06:21.510 --> 06:22.610
The heck?

06:22.610 --> 06:24.590
This isn't <i>NeriAli</i> at all!

06:24.590 --> 06:25.180
You said it.

06:25.180 --> 06:26.710
Um, excuse me.

06:26.710 --> 06:28.290
What, human girl?

06:28.290 --> 06:30.560
Is there some sort of festival going on?

06:30.560 --> 06:34.120
Why, we're celebrating the victory 
of our mighty leader, Chaos-sama!

06:34.120 --> 06:35.850
Huh? Why Chaos?

06:35.850 --> 06:36.620
What about Alice?

06:36.620 --> 06:38.830
Alice-pi and her slimy 
weasels are right there!

06:38.830 --> 06:40.330
<b>HERE LIES
\hALICE</b>

06:38.830 --> 06:40.330
<b>HERE LIES
\hIRON MONTY</b>

06:38.830 --> 06:40.330
<b>HERE LIES
\h\hOPIE</b>

06:40.660 --> 06:42.520
Alice! Iron Monty! Opie!

06:42.520 --> 06:43.550
What happened to them?

06:43.550 --> 06:44.310
They're dead!

06:44.310 --> 06:45.440
Huh? No way!

06:45.440 --> 06:46.670
Su-chan's missing.

06:46.670 --> 06:49.830
Is this a festival under the pretense 
that Alice and the others died?

06:49.830 --> 06:51.780
Ignorance sure is a scary thing!

06:51.780 --> 06:54.120
Ali-li-lice tried to fight 
back with hasami shogi,

06:54.120 --> 06:56.640
only to have the tables turned 
on her with gunjin shogi!

06:54.350 --> 06:56.640
<b>HERE LIES ALICE</b>

06:56.640 --> 06:58.370
That's what we're celebrating tonight!

06:58.370 --> 06:58.970
You're lying!

06:58.970 --> 07:00.220
Here's the proof!

07:00.220 --> 07:02.970
See what happens to the 
Darkizumites who defy us!

07:02.970 --> 07:04.360
Huh? Where are they?

07:07.450 --> 07:08.590
No, no, no!

07:08.590 --> 07:10.850
This would never happen in <i>NeriAli</i>!

07:10.850 --> 07:12.310
All right, fine.

07:12.310 --> 07:14.690
The four of you, tell these kids 
how it went down!

07:15.250 --> 07:17.900
Jonidan, silver-general-turned-engineer.

07:17.900 --> 07:21.590
I ensnared that torture-loving freak in a trap
and subjected him to torture.

07:21.590 --> 07:24.830
Knight-turned-cavalry, Quarter the Cicada.

07:24.830 --> 07:27.840
I kicked that no-good druggie to death!

07:27.840 --> 07:31.250
I, Guilt Incarnate, lance-turned-spy,

07:31.250 --> 07:33.290
launched a sneak attack on the noose girl.

07:33.290 --> 07:35.260
But she got away from me at the last moment.

07:35.260 --> 07:35.970
I'm sorry!

07:35.970 --> 07:38.100
Gold-general-turned-mine reporting in.

07:38.100 --> 07:41.010
I killed Alice in an explosion!

07:40.060 --> 07:56.580
<b></b>Chaos-sama in
Chaos Land\h

07:41.010 --> 07:42.630
This isn't <i>NeriAli</i> at all!

07:42.630 --> 07:43.780
That's right.

07:43.780 --> 07:45.820
You're in <i>Chaos-sama in Chaos Land</i> now.

07:45.820 --> 07:48.790
A magical kingdom you can enter 
but never leave.

07:49.250 --> 07:50.560
Sucks to be you.

07:50.560 --> 07:50.950
Huh?

07:50.950 --> 07:52.710
What's all this nonsense you made up?

07:52.710 --> 07:53.420
Whatever!

07:53.420 --> 07:55.310
This place isn't <i>NeriAli</i> at all!

07:55.310 --> 07:57.140
Let's head to Ikebukuro already!

07:57.840 --> 07:58.910
Death for you!

07:58.910 --> 08:00.380
Sorry, that's a death sentence.

08:00.380 --> 08:01.320
Death to them!

08:01.320 --> 08:01.870
Death penalty.

08:06.310 --> 08:08.270
Huh? Where are you from?

08:08.270 --> 08:09.840
You cocky little kids.

08:09.840 --> 08:10.600
Agano.

08:10.600 --> 08:12.180
And where are you going?

08:12.180 --> 08:13.550
We told you, Ikebukuro!

08:13.550 --> 08:15.470
I can't let you do that.

08:15.470 --> 08:19.070
Someone who's a real pain told me 
not to let anyone through.

08:19.070 --> 08:20.420
All of you, capture them!

08:20.740 --> 08:22.430
No more failures!

08:22.430 --> 08:24.390
Like that time with the animal!

08:24.390 --> 08:25.370
What now?

08:25.370 --> 08:26.360
What do you mean, "what now?"

08:26.360 --> 08:27.940
For now, we need to run away!

08:35.910 --> 08:37.110
I know, the escalator!

08:37.110 --> 08:38.280
What about it?

08:38.280 --> 08:40.410
You know, in the real <i>NeriAli</i>,

08:40.410 --> 08:43.080
this is where the entrance to Dark Nerima is.

08:43.080 --> 08:43.910
Oh, I get it!

08:43.910 --> 08:47.410
You mean, it might let us 
find a place to hide out!

08:48.960 --> 08:50.580
Oh, bingo!

08:50.580 --> 08:52.950
Just like in the show! I'm impressed.

08:52.950 --> 08:53.820
And, and!

08:53.820 --> 08:57.350
Beyond here lies a world of oddities!

08:57.350 --> 08:58.050
Spare us!

08:58.050 --> 08:59.010
We're nobodies!

08:59.010 --> 09:00.290
We have nothing here.

09:00.290 --> 09:01.320
Where are we?

09:01.310 --> 09:04.140
<b>12-Cheese</b>

09:01.310 --> 09:04.140
<b>Beef Bowl</b>

09:01.310 --> 09:04.140
<b>Medium: 480 yen
(tax included)</b>

09:01.310 --> 09:04.140
<b>Large: 600 yen
(tax included)</b>

09:01.310 --> 09:04.140
<b>Mozzarella  Samsø  Cheddar  Gorgonzola


Camembert  Coulommiers  Chaource  Gouda


Raclette  Valençay  Pecorino  String Cheese</b>

09:01.310 --> 09:04.140
<b>Beef Bowl
\h
Scrambled Egg
and Beef Bowl
Beef Plate
\h
Salad
Raw Egg</b>

09:01.310 --> 09:04.140
<b>M 320 yen
L 400 yen
M 380 yen
L 460 yen
M 260 yen
L 340 yen
80 yen
50 yen</b>

09:01.310 --> 09:04.140
<b>WE DON'T
SERVE
PORK
BOWLS</b>

09:01.320 --> 09:02.940
What are you doing here?

09:02.940 --> 09:05.390
We're just hiding, 
so please don't rat us out.

09:05.390 --> 09:07.470
Huh, a secret hideout?

09:07.470 --> 09:09.220
A resistance group! So cool!

09:09.220 --> 09:10.290
We wouldn't dare.

09:10.290 --> 09:12.410
Hey, hey. Why'd all this happen?

09:12.410 --> 09:16.210
I thought the Darkizumites were 
living happy lives with Alice.

09:16.210 --> 09:20.830
We were, but the shogi bag trapping 
the bad guys inside suddenly tore open,

09:20.830 --> 09:22.090
and out came Chaos and the others.

09:22.090 --> 09:24.540
Then Chaos took over in no time, 
and now we're here!

09:24.540 --> 09:25.930
It's been like this for a week!

09:25.930 --> 09:28.380
So this all happened recently?

09:28.380 --> 09:29.640
Why all of a sudden?

09:32.660 --> 09:33.270
What's that?

09:33.270 --> 09:34.560
Nothing, nothing!

09:34.560 --> 09:35.460
How fishy.

09:39.160 --> 09:41.880
Don't kill me, don't kill me, don't kill me!

09:41.300 --> 09:43.310
It's Su-chan!

09:43.310 --> 09:44.140
I'm so happy!

09:44.140 --> 09:45.680
Can you autograph this? Please!

09:46.160 --> 09:47.180
Are you going to kill me?

09:47.180 --> 09:49.050
No, we're not!

09:49.050 --> 09:52.760
So the folks of Dark Oizumi 
gave you a place to hide, Su-chan?

09:53.670 --> 09:54.700
Who are you?

09:54.700 --> 09:55.960
Just a passing stranger.

09:55.960 --> 09:58.020
They're after us, just like you.

09:58.020 --> 10:00.400
Hey, is it true that Alice 
and the rest are dead?

10:01.100 --> 10:03.800
It's more like they disappeared 
instead of died.

10:03.800 --> 10:05.720
Like in <i>The Human Vapor</i>?

10:05.720 --> 10:08.640
They got ambushed in gunjin shogi 
and went kaboom.

10:08.640 --> 10:09.400
"Kaboom"?

10:09.400 --> 10:11.010
Literal explosions.

10:11.010 --> 10:15.490
I managed to run away, but the 
other three ended up as shards.

10:15.490 --> 10:16.310
Shards?

10:16.310 --> 10:20.120
If the shards still exist, we can bring 
Alice and the others back to life.

10:20.120 --> 10:22.670
That's why Chaos sealed the shards away.

10:22.670 --> 10:23.550
Where?

10:23.550 --> 10:24.530
Their graves.

10:24.530 --> 10:25.440
I see.

10:25.430 --> 10:29.190
<b>HERE LIES
\hALICE</b>

10:25.430 --> 10:29.190
<b>HERE LIES
\hIRON MONTY</b>

10:25.430 --> 10:29.190
<b>HERE LIES
\h\hOPIE</b>

10:25.440 --> 10:29.650
You need the special scythe that the 
gravedigger has to open a grave, right?

10:29.190 --> 10:34.190
<b>Signature Gutton Candy</b>

10:29.190 --> 10:34.190
<b>Signature Gutton Candy</b>

10:29.650 --> 10:31.620
I saw the gravedigger running a stall.

10:31.620 --> 10:32.820
Ah, I remember him.

10:32.820 --> 10:34.180
Bring the shards, and...

10:34.510 --> 10:35.620
Oh, I know!

10:35.620 --> 10:36.440
Exactly.

10:36.440 --> 10:39.170
Place the shards in the legendary 
Fountain of Captured Pieces,

10:39.170 --> 10:40.410
and it'll bring them back to life.

10:40.410 --> 10:41.720
Wait a minute.

10:41.720 --> 10:44.670
Isn't that what they used before 
to bring Man-Cow back?

10:44.670 --> 10:47.250
In the book, they said it's pretty risky.

10:47.250 --> 10:49.710
Risky or not, it's the only option we have!

10:49.710 --> 10:52.980
So you mean we steal the 
gravedigger's scythe by force,

10:52.980 --> 10:54.500
open up the graves by force,

10:54.500 --> 10:57.770
and bring the shards to the Fountain 
of Captured Pieces by force...

10:57.770 --> 10:59.510
And hooray, Alice is back!

10:59.510 --> 11:01.610
Where was the Fountain 
of Captured Pieces, again?

11:01.610 --> 11:03.430
In Chaos's holiday home.

11:03.430 --> 11:04.630
That sounds impossible.

11:04.630 --> 11:06.080
Not an issue. Take a look.

11:06.080 --> 11:08.490
We risked our lives to steal this 
from his holiday home.

11:08.490 --> 11:11.000
We swapped it out with 
diluted iodine tincture.

11:11.000 --> 11:13.580
Swimming in <i>that</i> will sting you 
right in the you-know-where.

11:13.580 --> 11:15.130
I don't really get it, but sure!

11:15.130 --> 11:16.450
I'm all pumped up!

11:19.770 --> 11:20.560
Who goes there?!

11:20.560 --> 11:22.380
What a rude question, gano!

11:22.380 --> 11:25.080
Walker N501Y accompanied 
by four others, gano!

11:25.080 --> 11:25.760
Agano.

11:25.760 --> 11:26.650
Higashi-Agano.

11:26.650 --> 11:27.710
Nishi-Agano.

11:27.710 --> 11:29.020
Musashi-Agano!

11:29.020 --> 11:30.350
Oh, I do apologize.

11:30.350 --> 11:30.990
So, how goes it?

11:30.990 --> 11:32.400
Everything normal, gano.

11:32.400 --> 11:34.140
Nice and chaotic, koma.

11:34.140 --> 11:35.000
Bushi bushi.

11:35.000 --> 11:35.740
Iruma.

11:35.740 --> 11:36.660
Kotesashi!

11:36.660 --> 11:37.960
Sugamo Prison.

11:39.060 --> 11:40.410
Sugamo Prison.

11:40.410 --> 11:41.870
Pri-pri-prison.

11:41.870 --> 11:43.120
Hey, mister, what'll it run me?

11:43.120 --> 11:44.360
Didja hit yer head?

11:44.360 --> 11:46.260
It's all free on account of our victory!

11:46.260 --> 11:47.760
A batty beetle knows better!

11:47.760 --> 11:49.550
We'll take five freshly made ones, then!

11:49.550 --> 11:51.160
Okay, five it is.

11:51.160 --> 11:53.050
Been squeezing out entrails for thirty years.

11:53.050 --> 11:54.940
So delicious, they're practically to die for.

11:54.940 --> 11:56.370
Actually, just die! Die!

11:56.370 --> 11:58.390
Wow! You're an expert at this, mister!

11:58.390 --> 11:59.320
You bet yer sweet bottom!

11:59.320 --> 12:00.800
Make mine even bigger!

12:00.800 --> 12:01.950
The next Chaos right here!

12:01.950 --> 12:03.320
Fujimidai!

12:03.320 --> 12:04.490
Fujimidai!

12:04.490 --> 12:06.360
Okay, let's really get 'er going!

12:06.620 --> 12:08.240
Pile 'er on high!

12:11.160 --> 12:13.260
Why's this gone haywire?

12:14.910 --> 12:17.830
A niño like me working entrails 
for fifty years, slipping up?

12:17.830 --> 12:18.630
Pwha?!

12:20.000 --> 12:28.400
Tokorozawa-zawa! Tokorozawa-zawa!

12:28.400 --> 12:30.800
Doing this feels wrong.

12:28.400 --> 12:41.150
Tokorozawa-zawa! Tokorozawa-zawa!

12:30.800 --> 12:32.660
Do it like you're beheading them for real.

12:32.660 --> 12:33.990
Here I go!

12:38.430 --> 12:39.200
What's this?

12:39.200 --> 12:40.150
A shard.

12:40.150 --> 12:41.160
Not what I expected.

12:41.160 --> 12:45.880
Tokorozawa-zawa! Tokorozawa-zawa!

12:45.860 --> 12:50.840
Tokorozawa-zawa! Tokorozawa-zawa!

12:46.150 --> 12:47.740
Okay, let's book it!

12:50.260 --> 12:51.790
Yay! It really worked.

12:51.790 --> 12:52.850
I owe you all for this.

12:52.850 --> 12:53.950
Thanks.

12:57.890 --> 12:59.000
Eureekus!

12:59.000 --> 13:00.600
It's the suicidal girl!

13:00.600 --> 13:02.090
Sorry! Prepare yourself!

13:04.620 --> 13:05.380
Ouch!

13:04.860 --> 13:06.210
Sorry!

13:05.380 --> 13:06.630
Su-chan, hurry!

13:09.110 --> 13:10.450
Oh, Alice!

13:10.450 --> 13:11.560
Iron Monty!

13:11.560 --> 13:12.130
Opie...

13:12.130 --> 13:13.460
How can you tell?

13:13.460 --> 13:14.470
From their scent.

13:19.530 --> 13:21.520
Sorry, but what are you doing?!

13:21.520 --> 13:23.440
Sheesh, I'm fed up with this!

13:31.780 --> 13:32.810
What? What happened?!

13:32.810 --> 13:33.440
Oh, no!

13:33.440 --> 13:34.340
They're dead, dead, dead!

13:34.340 --> 13:35.300
But why?!

13:35.300 --> 13:36.820
Did we steal the wrong stuff?!

13:36.820 --> 13:37.850
There's absolutely no way!

13:37.850 --> 13:40.360
Did they change the settings on 
the Fountain of Captured Pieces?

13:40.360 --> 13:41.630
And who exactly did <i>that</i>?!

13:41.630 --> 13:43.010
Don't ask <i>me</i>!

13:49.480 --> 13:51.920
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

13:51.920 --> 13:52.990
Wh-What do we do?!

13:52.990 --> 13:53.400
There!

13:53.400 --> 13:55.090
Reimi-chan, you're making it worse!

14:03.280 --> 14:04.340
Su-chan!

14:04.340 --> 14:06.950
Su-chan, our last hope, is gone!

14:06.950 --> 14:08.550
It's all over!

14:13.070 --> 14:15.040
O! H! V!

14:17.160 --> 14:18.750
We're done for!

14:17.620 --> 14:19.340
It's no use! It's over!

14:18.750 --> 14:20.750
They'll kill all of us!

14:20.160 --> 14:22.050
The end! Fin! Finito!

14:21.130 --> 14:22.770
It's too early to give up!

14:22.770 --> 14:24.680
Yeah, I'm sure we can make things work...

14:24.080 --> 14:25.610
Spare us your fake concern!

14:25.610 --> 14:26.570
It's the end for all of us!

14:26.570 --> 14:27.830
Alice!

14:27.040 --> 14:28.810
That's not true!

14:33.980 --> 14:35.350
Snap out of it already!

14:36.460 --> 14:39.130
Alice and her friends are gone for good!

14:39.130 --> 14:41.780
You can't change what's already happened!

14:41.780 --> 14:44.210
It's too late for all these regrets!

14:44.210 --> 14:45.230
It's all over!

14:45.720 --> 14:51.640
There's no point in thinking over and over 
about what you could have done after the fact.

14:53.030 --> 14:54.490
<b>Entrance
Ceremony</b>

14:58.510 --> 15:02.130
So instead, let's think about what 
we can do now—and act on it.

15:05.510 --> 15:06.980
Alice.

15:06.980 --> 15:08.230
She's just like Alice.

15:08.230 --> 15:09.550
The spitting image of her.

15:10.230 --> 15:13.510
She might be able to bring us 
back to the old, fun times!

15:13.510 --> 15:14.030
Hey!

15:14.030 --> 15:14.880
Yeah!

15:14.890 --> 15:16.220
Voila!

15:16.430 --> 15:18.010
Alice left these behind.

15:18.010 --> 15:18.710
Go on!

15:18.710 --> 15:19.860
What do you mean, "go on"?

15:19.860 --> 15:21.070
Wait, are those the real deal?

15:21.070 --> 15:21.720
I wanna try 'em on!

15:21.720 --> 15:24.430
You're the only one who can save Dark Oizumi!

15:24.430 --> 15:25.960
We've been waiting for you!

15:25.960 --> 15:26.530
No, I'm not!

15:26.530 --> 15:27.640
Go on, just change.

15:26.970 --> 15:28.870
I'll cover their eyes!

15:27.640 --> 15:28.710
Hey, wait!

15:28.710 --> 15:30.700
I get it! I can dress myself!

15:29.180 --> 15:30.420
Go on!

15:34.670 --> 15:35.670
She looks just like her!

15:35.670 --> 15:36.220
A dead ringer!

15:36.220 --> 15:38.310
A little chubby, but otherwise perfect!

15:38.310 --> 15:38.990
Chubby?!

15:38.990 --> 15:40.390
I'm so jealous...

15:40.970 --> 15:42.620
P! C! R!

15:42.620 --> 15:43.930
Looking at them closely...

15:43.930 --> 15:44.600
There's a resemblance.

15:44.600 --> 15:46.440
Squint and they look like the real thing.

15:46.440 --> 15:47.090
Dead ringers.

15:47.610 --> 15:49.360
Opie and Iron Monty!

15:49.360 --> 15:50.120
Yeah, right!

15:50.120 --> 15:51.890
I, for one, am flattered.

15:51.890 --> 15:52.630
No fair!

15:52.630 --> 15:53.840
What about me, then?

15:53.840 --> 15:54.940
Su-chan, I guess.

15:54.940 --> 15:55.540
You guess?!

15:55.540 --> 15:56.300
We're begging you!

15:56.610 --> 15:57.780
How wonderful!

15:57.780 --> 15:58.300
Perfection.

15:58.300 --> 16:00.110
Aren't these just cosplay?

16:00.110 --> 16:01.560
Powers not included, right?

16:01.560 --> 16:02.680
Rest assured.

16:02.680 --> 16:05.610
I'm sure that we were normal 
humans like you in the past.

16:05.610 --> 16:09.380
But now, we're Darkizumites in body 
and mind, overdependency and all.

16:09.380 --> 16:12.210
So dressing up like that might just 
give you their powers, too!

16:13.070 --> 16:14.690
I apologize, but prepare yourselves!

16:16.460 --> 16:18.760
Sorry, what is this? Sorry!

16:18.760 --> 16:20.600
This is pickled ginger juice!

16:20.600 --> 16:21.200
My eyes sting!

16:21.480 --> 16:22.830
Now's your chance!

16:27.720 --> 16:28.620
Where are we?

16:28.620 --> 16:37.250
Check! Check! Check!

16:31.190 --> 16:34.720
Seize them! Time for some tough love!

16:37.250 --> 16:38.540
Oh, yeah, Nadeko-chan.

16:38.540 --> 16:40.310
That thing on your skirt.

16:40.310 --> 16:41.240
It turns into a bow!

16:41.240 --> 16:41.950
This thing?

16:41.950 --> 16:42.710
That's right.

16:42.710 --> 16:45.770
It's a multi-weapon that the Horsehair 
Worm Man made from an umbrella!

16:45.770 --> 16:47.280
I don't have any arrows, though.

16:47.280 --> 16:48.770
We're surrounded by grave markers!

16:48.770 --> 16:49.410
What?

16:49.410 --> 16:50.580
Isn't that bad karma?

16:50.580 --> 16:54.360
Karmic retribution stopped being 
a thing after 7G. Probably...

16:54.360 --> 16:56.240
You really think so?

16:56.240 --> 16:58.370
I don't know who you are, but sorry!

17:02.780 --> 17:04.380
Agano archery's something else.

17:04.380 --> 17:07.920
Sorry, but prepare yourselves!

17:08.280 --> 17:09.230
Huh?

17:14.220 --> 17:16.740
A lance, and now a knight?

17:16.740 --> 17:17.800
That's not gunjin shogi!

17:18.070 --> 17:19.840
What are you spineless cowards doing?

17:19.840 --> 17:21.010
You're on a battlefield!

17:21.010 --> 17:22.980
Bring a little more chaos!

17:36.450 --> 17:37.870
That hurts!

17:43.280 --> 17:44.140
I've figured it out!

17:44.140 --> 17:45.450
Figured what out?

17:45.450 --> 17:47.580
They're all following the rules of shogi!

17:47.580 --> 17:49.550
I don't know how to play shogi!

17:49.890 --> 17:52.500
I'm starting to feel like none 
of this is chaotic at all.

17:52.500 --> 17:53.290
Shizuru-chan!

17:53.290 --> 17:54.700
Calico Cat is a shogi gold general!

17:54.700 --> 17:55.290
So what?

17:55.290 --> 17:56.950
Gold generals can't move 
diagonally backwards!

17:56.950 --> 17:57.980
I see. No wonder!

18:03.720 --> 18:04.770
<b>HERE LIES
\h\hCALICO CAT</b>

18:04.760 --> 18:06.740
Wow, you're amazing, Akira-chan.

18:06.740 --> 18:09.330
Sorry, sorry, sorry!

18:08.400 --> 18:11.180
Guilt Incarnate was a lance, wasn't he?

18:12.020 --> 18:13.440
Sorry!

18:15.080 --> 18:18.900
Tottari, tottari, tottari!

18:16.350 --> 18:18.200
Hey, stop, you creep!

18:18.900 --> 18:19.710
Reimi!

18:19.710 --> 18:20.980
Jonidan is a silver general,

18:20.980 --> 18:23.500
so his weak spots are directly 
to his left, right, and back!

18:31.750 --> 18:32.130
<b>HERE LIES
JONIDAN</b>

18:31.910 --> 18:34.470
Agano archery target leading 
should handle a jumping knight.

18:39.460 --> 18:40.800
Nice swing!

18:40.800 --> 18:43.680
Nice swing! Nice swing!

18:46.100 --> 18:52.020
No prob, no prob, no prob, no prob!

18:52.020 --> 18:52.910
Game set.

18:55.310 --> 18:56.470
Now!

19:01.530 --> 19:01.820
<b>HERE LIES
MAN-COW</b>

19:09.860 --> 19:11.060
I knew it.

19:11.060 --> 19:13.260
They may be shogi pieces, 
but they go down like dominoes.

19:13.260 --> 19:14.170
Run away!

19:17.160 --> 19:19.360
Anything but that!

19:19.360 --> 19:20.560
I can't take this!

19:20.560 --> 19:22.090
Run for it!

19:22.090 --> 19:23.090
Hey!

19:23.090 --> 19:25.610
Don't leave the king behind and 
run away, you stupid pawns!

19:28.190 --> 19:30.450
Hey, we know what's going on, Chaos.

19:30.450 --> 19:33.180
You say chaos this, chaos that, 
but you're not chaotic at all.

19:33.180 --> 19:35.400
It looks like you can't 
escape the rules of shogi.

19:35.400 --> 19:38.550
So you're just a lapdog that dreams of chaos.

19:38.550 --> 19:39.460
How sad.

19:39.460 --> 19:39.970
Shut up!

19:39.970 --> 19:40.870
I'm plenty chaotic!

19:40.870 --> 19:43.480
Besides, a game of shogi 
without any pawns is a lost cause!

19:43.480 --> 19:44.580
Give it up already!

19:44.580 --> 19:49.240
Kill him! Kill him!

19:47.060 --> 19:47.990
Tokiwaman!

19:47.990 --> 19:49.240
Add to subscription!

19:49.240 --> 19:50.470
Grab him!

19:54.930 --> 19:58.110
That sure is an old-looking design 
that doesn't fit with <i>NeriAli</i>.

19:58.110 --> 19:59.590
Look at what you've done!

19:59.590 --> 20:02.230
The Witch Queen of Ikebukuro 
will hear about this!

20:02.230 --> 20:04.800
Yoka-hime will not tolerate your actions!

20:05.450 --> 20:06.810
Yoka?

20:06.810 --> 20:08.890
By "Yoka-hime," do you mean Yoka?

20:08.890 --> 20:10.300
Nakatomi Yoka?!

20:10.300 --> 20:13.670
Yeah! You sure do know a lot 
for a bunch of backwater hicks!

20:13.670 --> 20:15.710
Of course we know her! She's our friend!

20:15.710 --> 20:17.500
We're going to Ikebukuro to meet her!

20:17.500 --> 20:18.090
What?!

20:18.090 --> 20:20.740
She'd never give you insolent 
punks the time of day!

20:20.740 --> 20:22.200
She's Yoka, the Witch Queen!

20:22.200 --> 20:25.380
The fearsome ruler of Ikebukuro, 
not to mention the entire world!

20:25.380 --> 20:26.150
You're lying!

20:26.150 --> 20:27.860
You'll all be turned into egg custard!

20:27.860 --> 20:29.320
Serves you right!

20:29.320 --> 20:30.930
Must report, must report!

20:32.050 --> 20:34.490
What does he mean by Witch Queen?

20:35.360 --> 20:38.320
That said, now we know Yoka-chan is safe.

20:38.320 --> 20:39.120
That's true.

20:39.120 --> 20:41.420
Chaos must have been bluffing.

20:42.680 --> 20:44.710
Thank you!

20:44.710 --> 20:47.530
Now Oizumi-gakuen can finally be at peace!

20:47.530 --> 20:53.220
Please continue to watch over us 
for eternity, Queen Alice-sama.

20:53.220 --> 20:55.030
What? No can do.

20:55.750 --> 20:58.240
We need to head over to Ikebukuro.

20:58.240 --> 20:59.960
Who will be our ruler, then?!

20:59.960 --> 21:01.150
Take care of it yourselves.

21:01.150 --> 21:02.970
We have dependency issues, you know!

21:02.970 --> 21:05.020
What if the Walkers come 
back to settle the score?!

21:05.020 --> 21:05.670
Good luck.

21:05.670 --> 21:06.870
I'm sure you can handle it.

21:06.870 --> 21:07.840
How irresponsible!

21:07.840 --> 21:08.610
Are we really?

21:08.610 --> 21:10.310
Whatever. Just give us back our clothes.

21:10.310 --> 21:11.280
Hey, wait...

21:21.970 --> 21:23.290
You know...

21:23.290 --> 21:28.470
The 7G incident has to be the reason that 
the town became <i>NeriAli</i> World, right?

21:28.470 --> 21:32.240
Then, out of nowhere, 
Chaos and the Walkers came back

21:32.240 --> 21:34.620
and turned it into Bad Guy World.

21:34.620 --> 21:37.150
Why did that happen 
after they were fine for so long?

21:37.150 --> 21:40.370
Someone deliberately tampered 
with the world of <i>NeriAli</i>?

21:40.370 --> 21:41.520
But why?

21:41.520 --> 21:42.520
I'm not sure.

21:42.520 --> 21:46.450
They gained gunjin shogi powers 
for a short amount of time,

21:46.450 --> 21:49.280
and the settings for the Fountain of 
Captured Pieces got changed, too.

21:49.280 --> 21:55.040
All these mysteries worry me, 
but what concerns me the most is still...

21:55.040 --> 21:56.040
Yeah.

21:56.040 --> 21:57.030
Of course.

22:04.790 --> 22:06.300
Yoka...

22:07.730 --> 22:09.340
the Witch Queen?
